  "configuration_id": "config_047",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_032 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted; acc=0.7250), with config_029 (concat fusion) very close at 0.7207. scgpt is clearly inferior (0.5200), and imagenet_vit_l + transformer dominates resnet50 + avgpool. However, the RNA encoder dimension remains underexplored—only scvi_n200 and scgpt have been tested. Question: config_047 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) isolates the RNA encoder choice by swapping scvi_n200 for PCA while keeping all other parameters at their best-known values. This tests whether a simple linear projection can match or exceed the learned scVI latent space in the strongest architecture. Why this is the best use: With 4 experiments remaining, resolving whether PCA is competitive is the highest-information experiment—it either opens a new family of configurations to exploit or confirms scvi_n200 as essential, allowing the remaining budget to focus on fine-tuning the scvi_n200 + vit_l + transformer architecture (e.g., singleprofile variant, fusion ablation)."
}

